-- Northbridge Compliance Solutions Ltd: Packaging Data (POM) submissions.
-- 3 submissions: 2025 H1 (Large only, Accepted), 2025 H2 (mixed Large+Small, Accepted then
-- a resubmission already in progress with a new file uploaded and fees pending), 2026 H1
-- (Large only, Rejected). POM submissions are SubmissionType='Producer' in Cosmos/Synapse -
-- a distinct data source/journey from the Registration submissions seeded above (different
-- event chain, half-year SubmissionPeriod, rpd.Pom instead of rpd.CompanyDetails for the
-- per-member data rows).

if not exists (select 1 from rpd.Submissions where SubmissionId = N'8447509F-A90E-4436-BB34-06CDDE1C7AB9')
begin
    -- rpd.Pom: 3 varied packaging rows per member per file (materials Plastic/Paper-Card/Glass).
    -- 2025 H1 (Large only)

    -- 2025 H2 original file (mixed Large+Small)

    -- 2025 H2 resubmission file (mixed Large+Small, corrected figures)

    -- 2026 H1 (Large only). Cycle A = original file, Accepted (FileName 62D90EC6-...). Cycle B =
    -- corrected file submitted later, Rejected - the current/latest state (FileName B52AAEE6-...).

    -- cosmos_file_metadata: 1 row per uploaded file (5 files across the 3 submissions - 2025 H2
    -- has 2 files: the original submission and the in-progress resubmission upload; 2026 H1 has
    -- 2 files: an original file that was Accepted, and a later corrected file that was Rejected).

    -- SubmissionEvents: Accepted chain = AntivirusCheck -> AntivirusResult -> CheckSplitter ->
    -- ProducerValidation -> Submitted -> RegulatorPoMDecision. 2025 H2 additionally has a
    -- resubmission-in-progress tail: PackagingResubmissionReferenceNumberCreated -> a fresh
    -- AntivirusCheck/AntivirusResult/CheckSplitter/ProducerValidation/Submitted for the newly
    -- uploaded file -> PackagingResubmissionFeeViewed (fee ready to view/pay, not yet paid or
    -- finally submitted - deliberately no PackagingDataResubmissionFeePayment or
    -- PackagingResubmissionApplicationSubmitted event).
    -- 2025 H1 (SubmissionId 8447509F-A90E-4436-BB34-06CDDE1C7AB9) - Accepted

    -- 2025 H2 (SubmissionId C18BF17E-DEC1-434E-A5CA-A37D9811C72D) - Accepted, then resubmission in progress

    -- 2026 H1 (SubmissionId 84FA8B3B-ACF0-4FAE-8B70-27137AF5F24C) - two cycles under the same
    -- SubmissionId: Cycle A (FileId 68DD58D5-...) was submitted and Accepted; months later the
    -- compliance scheme submitted a corrected file, Cycle B (FileId 559469D2-...), which the
    -- regulator went on to Reject - the current/latest state. This mirrors the real packaging
    -- frontend's own resubmission routing (FileUploadSubLandingController.HandleSubmissionBasedOnStatus
    -- -> SubmissionService.IsAnySubmissionAcceptedForDataPeriod), which only shows the "Resubmit
    -- packaging data" intermediate page for a submission whose own history contains an Accepted
    -- decision - a submission that has only ever been Rejected falls through to the plain
    -- first-time upload flow instead. Deliberately no PackagingResubmissionReferenceNumberCreated
    -- event for either cycle - that only appears once the newer fee-based resubmission journey is
    -- actually started, and its absence is what keeps this submission routed to the intermediate
    -- page rather than skipped straight to the resubmission task list.

    -- Submissions: flattened final-state record, 1 row per submission.

end

